      { id: 'moon', label: 'Callisto', at: pc(230, 450), kicker: 'Galilean moon · the Green Zone', title: 'Callisto from orbit',
        html: '<p>The quietest of Jupiter’s big moons, and the busiest sky. It sits outside the main radiation belts, so baseline people can live here, and its old, cold crust is the steadiest ground at Jupiter. Fuel comes up from it, scoop catch goes down to it, and workers on rotation pass through one logistics node overhead.</p>',
